A||||15||qwikgta||Dropped my 88 coupe....b4 and after||||10||
Z||000000||qwikgta||10-08-2001||09:40 PM||||Here are some pics before and after.  I put on KYB's and cut the coils 1.33" front and 1.25" rear.  It will do for now, but I want it lower.  I also put on a 88 GT rear swaybar.  Poly is my winter project.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/000money_shot.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lowered_pic.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 66K, Header no Cat w/ Supertrapp, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, GT rear swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents, clear tails, KYB's, dropped springs.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject/robsfieroproject.html   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Brian87egotrip||10-08-2001||09:43 PM||||nice car.  I like the rims.<P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroMaster88||10-08-2001||09:49 PM||||OK!  That does it!  After seeing 2 people on the forum drop their 88's by cutting the springs I am gonna do it too!  One week from saturday when I have the weekend off I will lower my car.  This is gonnna be cool.  Give me some good advice and some ideas on how to make it "easier". <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">              <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||8
Z||000003||qwikgta||10-08-2001||10:09 PM||||The big ?? is how much to take off the coils, I have never worked on the suspension before so I was a little worried about it, but I just kept my chiltons and haynes manuals next to me and I was alright.  <BR>  For the front, my only prob was that I didn't know that the springs had to go in a certain way, I didn't realize that the bottom control arm has a little pocket for the spring to sit in, and I didn't put them in correctly the first time.  So I had to take it apart TWICE.  Now I could do it with my eyes closed.  I took off about one and 1/3 coil, I wish I had done more, but again I was not sure.  I got about a inch and 1/2 drop with it but I was looking for 2".  <BR>   For the rear taking them off was a breeze, both off in 30-45 min, but getting them on was a ***** .  I put on new KYB so I used a sping compresser and once the springs were off I cleaned them and cut them (about 1 coil and a quarter) (again I should have done more) I had no probs and I made sure that I had the spring in the little pocket on the bottom of the new strut, but then I didnt realize that the top of the strut has to be on a specific way.  The 3 bolts are not all the distance apart, it is not a perfect triangle of bolts, one is off set and that bolt needs to face 180 out from the front of the strut, I didn't put the tops on correct, so when I went to put the struts in the top three bolts were off by about 2 inches clockwise.  So again I had to take the spring compresser to the springs and turn the top plate about 45 deg.  Once that was done the drivers side went in with a few hammer blows to the top spindle bolt, the pass side WOULD NOT FIT, I spent over an hour trying to get the top spindle bolt to fit, I finally had to jack up the car suspension and have the strut going up into the bottom of the mount area and then work the top three bolts into the holes, it was a PITA.  <P>Well good luck, I wanted 2" drop so I would cut more like 2 coils front and 1 3/4 coil rear.  BUT DO THIS AT YOUR OWN RISK<P>Post pics when done.<P>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dgzfiero||10-08-2001||10:17 PM||||Looks good alot more of a drop than the eibach springs I tried to lower mine with.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AutoXdbdragSE||10-08-2001||11:21 PM||||Ummm... am i the only one that wonders which one is the dropped pic.. it only looks like a 1" drop?  1st pic, the front tire is even with the botom of the black trim. 2nd even with top, my black trim is only an 1" so what was all the work for???  i mean it looks good, but it isn't that much, can you go further, how far is too far, i'm interested in lowering my car, but it it is that much work for that little change, i just don't know||||reg||1
